## 3. Cross-device handshake mechanism smoke (real rig pairs)

Standalone harness /tmp/opencode/t7-smoke.cpp linked against build-t7's
liblsfg-vk-common.a exercising EXACTLY the primitives the handshake uses:

== direction 1: AMD exports -> Intel imports ==
  cycle 0..4: exported live fd=13 right after enqueue → import + fenced wait OK
== direction 2: Intel exports -> AMD imports ==
  cycle 0..4: exported live fd=13 right after enqueue → import + fenced wait OK
== -1 sentinel: queue-signal fallback == OK
SMOKE OK: all handshakes completed

Proven empirically:
(a) exportFd() immediately AFTER enqueueing the signal submit (no host wait)
    yields a LIVE sync fd on both RADV GFX1201 and ANV ARL — copy transference
    wraps the pending payload;
(b) temporary imports into a persistent ring slot work repeatedly across cycles
    in both cross-vendor directions;
(c) re-signaling a ring slot after its payload was consumed by a queue wait is
    legal across cycles (the recycling choreography is sound).

## 4. Handshake-mechanism summary (who signals what; fd flow)

Mode detection: backend compares instance-selected physdev deviceUUID() against
the gameDeviceUUID in-param of openContext (layer passes vk.deviceUUID()).
Equal/nullopt ⇒ SAME-device ⇒ imported-timeline protocol untouched. Differ ⇒
CROSS-device ⇒ SYNC_FD binary handshakes below. Mode stored in the context;
layer queries it via Instance::isCrossDevice(context) right after openContext.

Timeline value ↔ binary edge mapping (1:1, verified single-waiter today):

  VALUE (timeline)            CROSS-DEVICE EDGE (sync fd)
  layer capture signals L     EDGE-A "frame k captured":  layer → backend
  backend prepass waits L       layer capture-submit signals ring slot
                                [handshakeIdx % 2], exportFd() right after
                                enqueue, fd passed INTO scheduleFrames();
                                backend temporarily imports it into its own
                                ring slot and the prepass waits it.
  backend main_i signals L+1+i  EDGE-B "frame i done": backend → layer
  layer blit_i waits L+1+i      backend main_i signals doneSlots[i],
                                exportFd() right after enqueue, all done fds
                                RETURNED from scheduleFrames(); layer
                                temporarily imports doneFds[i] into
                                doneWaitSemaphores[i]; blit_i waits it.

Internal chains unchanged: backend prepass→mains stays a LOCAL timeline
semaphore (prepassSemaphore) in both modes; layer acquire/postCopy semaphore
pairs stay local binaries in both modes; renderFence/cmdbufFence stay plain
device-private fences (150 ms timeout pattern preserved; NO externalized
fences anywhere).

Recycling legality (binary semaphores must not be re-signaled while signaled):
- layer capture ring (size 2): capture(c) WAITS slot[(c-1)%2] in the same
  submit that signals slot[c%2] — consumes cycle c-1's leftover payload with
  zero extra submissions; first cycle skips the recycle-wait.
- backend done slots (size multiplier-1): prepass(c+1) waits ALL done slots of
  cycle c alongside the capture import — consumes leftovers before mains(c+1)
  re-signal them; first cycle skips (nothing signaled yet); never blocks since
  cmdbufFence(c) already ordered batch c complete.
- backend capture ring (size 2): temporary imports revert to unsignaled after
  the prepass wait observes them, so re-import two cycles later is legal.

Edge-fd timing constraint honored: every fd EXISTS before the waiter's submit
is enqueued — layer exports capture fd BEFORE calling scheduleFrames (capture
submit moved ahead of scheduleFrames in the cross branch only); backend
exports done fds inside scheduleFrames BEFORE returning them to the layer.

fd ownership: captureReadyFd transfers to the backend unconditionally at call
(import consumes on success; helper closes on failure); done fds remain owned
by the layer (import consumes each; FdJanitor closes unconsumed ones if the
blit loop throws; backend closes partial doneFds if scheduling throws).
Cross-mode swapchain ctor closes the unused exported timeline syncFd.

-1 sentinel ("already signaled"): layer passes it through; backend emulates by
queue-signaling the ring slot directly + DeviceWaitIdle (vkSignalSemaphoreKHR
on binary semaphores returns DEVICE_LOST on RADV/ANV — todo-3 finding). Layer
skips the blit wait entirely for a -1 done fd (frame already completed).

Ordering/coherence: the handshakes ARE the memory-ordering mechanism for the
dma-buf/opaque exchange images; image layout dualities untouched
(sourceImage TRANSFER_DST_OPTIMAL game-side vs GENERAL backend-side kept).
Pacing/present order/FIFO injection/shader chain untouched.

